      "scenario": "The scanner approves eleven independently executed leaking scripts. It cuts at a physical line starting exit/return even inside command substitution, after line continuation, or in a function declaration, and assumes a top-level return exits a script without errexit. Quote state resets per line, so << END inside a multiline string starts a fictitious heredoc and hides later allocations. An otherwise accepted own trap can be disabled by set -n, or fail on a 0000 descendant. All eleven pass the complete gate when substituted into a tracked path; ten also pass CI-warning ShellCheck.",
